1
00:00:00,041 --> 00:00:01,499
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,000
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,166 --> 00:00:05,125
(Episode 48)

4
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,500
Go inside, Yeong Ju.

5
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:31,489
You waited for Seung Hyun.
Why can't you wait for Seung Woo?

6
00:00:31,875 --> 00:00:33,250
Because he's sick.

7
00:00:34,638 --> 00:00:38,179
My mom was hard on me too,
but always went easy on Yu Ri.

8
00:00:38,574 --> 00:00:39,908
Maybe because she's the youngest.

9
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:42,375
By the way, how's Yu Ri doing?

10
00:00:43,125 --> 00:00:46,630
She lives in America. She cut me off.

11
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:48,875
She told her in-laws I was dead.

12
00:00:49,627 --> 00:00:53,086
- What?
- If I went after Cha Min Ki for money,

13
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:55,375
may lightning strike me right now.

14
00:00:55,625 --> 00:01:00,500
Even Sa Bin's sister-in-law thought
I was a total gold digger today.

15
00:01:01,476 --> 00:01:03,976
You've made up your mind now, right?

16
00:01:06,875 --> 00:01:08,875
You need to be sure this time.

17
00:01:09,125 --> 00:01:13,000
One son threatens to leave, so you refuse.
The other objects, so you give up.

18
00:01:13,041 --> 00:01:14,916
What kind of love is that?

19
00:01:15,125 --> 00:01:17,041
Don't you feel sorry for Sa Bin?

20
00:01:17,533 --> 00:01:20,533
- I'm closer to him than you are.
- No way.

21
00:01:21,041 --> 00:01:23,000
You can't be friends with Sa Bin anymore.

22
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:25,791
That's an order. I have the right. Got it?

23
00:01:27,504 --> 00:01:28,874
Answer me.

24
00:01:28,875 --> 00:01:32,040
Even though you knew him first,
I'm the one he's marrying.

25
00:01:32,041 --> 00:01:34,166
Fine.

26
00:01:34,625 --> 00:01:38,625
Seeing him today, I realized
Sa Bin only has eyes for you. Congrats.

27
00:01:39,171 --> 00:01:42,212
Still, you should respect friendship.

28
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:45,222
Love isn't all that matters.
Friendship matters too.

29
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,250
I need to make money fast
and move out of this house.

30
00:01:48,625 --> 00:01:50,000
Who's stopping you?

31
00:01:50,250 --> 00:01:52,499
Mom, the door!

32
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:54,916
Yeong Ju!

33
00:01:57,015 --> 00:01:58,489
Seung Woo.

34
00:01:58,490 --> 00:02:00,375
What's wrong? Did he get hurt?

35
00:02:00,708 --> 00:02:03,041
- Seung Woo.
- Watch out.

36
00:02:03,125 --> 00:02:06,375
What happened to him? Seung Woo!

37
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:08,916
Is his leg hurt?

38
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:11,500
Yes, he's okay.
He passed out from drinking.

39
00:02:11,541 --> 00:02:14,747
I should've gone out to check.
Get inside. Hurry.

40
00:02:18,125 --> 00:02:19,166
Watch out.

41
00:02:22,184 --> 00:02:25,309
Seung Woo, what happened to you?

42
00:02:26,375 --> 00:02:28,351
Seung Woo, are you okay?

43
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:32,541
Here.

44
00:02:53,290 --> 00:02:54,331
What's with you?

45
00:02:54,922 --> 00:02:55,922
What?

46
00:02:56,282 --> 00:02:58,948
Why did you come here
with Do Hee's fiancé?

47
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
He's not her fiancé. They broke up.

48
00:03:01,375 --> 00:03:04,916
Besides, there's nothing between us.
You promised not to assume things.

49
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,916
Anyone would find this suspicious.

50
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:12,136
Well, I should get going.

51
00:03:12,250 --> 00:03:14,839
Okay. Have a glass of water before you go.

52
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:17,580
Okay. I was actually thirsty.

53
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:22,066
Thank you so much.

54
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:24,000
Thanks, Director.

55
00:03:24,164 --> 00:03:26,539
I resigned. Just call me Ji Hu.

56
00:03:26,541 --> 00:03:29,250
You resigned? Why leave such a good job?

57
00:03:30,375 --> 00:03:31,375
It just happened.

58
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:35,625
It seems my mom overstepped again.

59
00:03:35,830 --> 00:03:37,580
Trust my uncle. Don't worry too much.

60
00:03:37,750 --> 00:03:39,390
My dad can't win against him.

61
00:03:39,915 --> 00:03:41,665
That's exactly my concern.

62
00:03:41,831 --> 00:03:43,706
I can't let them fight because of me...

63
00:03:44,074 --> 00:03:46,408
Will you wait for world peace
before you get married?

64
00:03:54,145 --> 00:03:55,397
That could've been awful.

65
00:03:55,770 --> 00:03:58,645
Without us, you'd still be waiting,
worried sick about him.

66
00:03:58,666 --> 00:04:00,375
That's right.

67
00:04:00,810 --> 00:04:02,874
Seung Woo has been through so much...

68
00:04:02,875 --> 00:04:05,750
You keep treating him like a baby.
That's why he still acts like one.

69
00:04:05,791 --> 00:04:07,041
Mom.

70
00:04:07,416 --> 00:04:08,416
What?

71
00:04:11,101 --> 00:04:12,310
I should get going.

72
00:04:13,750 --> 00:04:14,791
Thanks for everything.

73
00:04:16,166 --> 00:04:19,416
They're on their way out.
You don't have to see them off.

74
00:04:20,375 --> 00:04:21,666
Yeong Ju.

75
00:04:23,166 --> 00:04:25,791
- I think he's waking up.
- Yeong Ju.

76
00:04:28,125 --> 00:04:29,500
So much to do.

77
00:04:32,250 --> 00:04:35,250
Thank you for helping.
You must've been taken aback.

78
00:04:36,375 --> 00:04:37,500
I thought it was nice.

79
00:04:38,666 --> 00:04:41,638
- What?
- You and your mom arguing like that.

80
00:04:41,833 --> 00:04:42,833
I envy you.

81
00:04:44,166 --> 00:04:46,357
Only blood relatives can act that way.

82
00:04:47,125 --> 00:04:48,416
Because they can never really separate.

83
00:04:49,776 --> 00:04:51,826
Even if they part, their bond remains.

84
00:04:55,796 --> 00:04:57,349
Consider what I said earlier.

85
00:04:58,795 --> 00:05:00,041
Ji Hu.

86
00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:02,833
Whether we were born rich or poor,

87
00:05:03,125 --> 00:05:05,125
we're old enough to stop
depending on our parents.

88
00:05:05,539 --> 00:05:07,289
Let's build something of our own.

89
00:05:07,838 --> 00:05:10,416
The art we want to draw
and the projects we want to create.

90
00:05:13,666 --> 00:05:15,947
I'm happy our goals align.

91
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,250
I should go. Go inside.

92
00:05:36,658 --> 00:05:39,994
It's pretty but empty inside.
Just like me.

93
00:05:43,166 --> 00:05:46,125
Everyone thinks I have it all
because of my family,

94
00:05:47,251 --> 00:05:48,616
but I've always felt empty.

95
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:52,075
So I want to change that now.

96
00:05:53,364 --> 00:05:54,948
Will you help me, Ji Ni?

97
00:05:57,671 --> 00:05:58,977
Help you with what?

98
00:05:59,443 --> 00:06:01,525
Would you consider
making children's books again?

99
00:06:02,572 --> 00:06:05,613
I love the strength in your illustrations.
I want to work with you.

100
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,000
I made that decision at the beach.

101
00:06:29,232 --> 00:06:30,316
Mom.

102
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:32,375
- Yeah?
- Are you feeling any better?

103
00:06:33,375 --> 00:06:34,625
Not at all.

104
00:06:36,375 --> 00:06:38,750
Your uncle is driving me crazy.

105
00:06:39,317 --> 00:06:40,651
Late-life romance is no joke.

106
00:06:41,666 --> 00:06:44,750
Please let him follow his heart.
He's never done this before.

107
00:06:45,567 --> 00:06:47,067
He'll be hurt if you oppose him.

108
00:06:53,375 --> 00:06:56,250
There's a limit to everything.
That feels good.

109
00:06:57,770 --> 00:07:01,520
Your hands really are magic. Thank you.

110
00:07:02,546 --> 00:07:03,716
I heard you two were schoolmates.

111
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:05,999
You seem to have a special connection.

112
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,541
More like an ill-fated one.

113
00:07:08,375 --> 00:07:13,000
A schoolmate will be my sister-in-law?
Does that even make sense?

114
00:07:13,903 --> 00:07:17,139
Still, that's better
than uncle spending his whole life alone.

115
00:07:18,750 --> 00:07:20,250
Did he ask you to convince me?

116
00:07:20,291 --> 00:07:21,500
Come on, Mom.

117
00:07:24,158 --> 00:07:25,158
Does that feel good?

118
00:07:25,875 --> 00:07:26,875
I don't know.

119
00:07:30,344 --> 00:07:32,678
I'll take your advice, Dad,
and run the publishing company.

120
00:07:33,416 --> 00:07:34,999
If you trust me with it,
I'll give it my all.

121
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,791
Really? That's great.

122
00:07:37,332 --> 00:07:39,873
Why are you being so formal?
You don't need to ask me to trust you.

123
00:07:39,875 --> 00:07:41,500
Of course I trust you. You're my son.

124
00:07:41,666 --> 00:07:43,000
Did I sound like that?

125
00:07:44,789 --> 00:07:46,914
I always wanted to be a soldier
like you, Dad.

126
00:07:47,796 --> 00:07:51,296
Your uniform and discipline made you
look so impressive.

127
00:07:52,033 --> 00:07:54,074
I used to imitate the way you spoke.

128
00:07:54,250 --> 00:07:55,250
Really?

129
00:07:56,041 --> 00:07:58,750
Going to Geoje Island brought back
even more memories.

130
00:07:59,125 --> 00:08:02,250
I wanted you to be a soldier too,
but I loved your piano playing.

131
00:08:02,750 --> 00:08:04,166
I don't have that kind of talent.

132
00:08:04,375 --> 00:08:06,791
I wanted to keep playing to the end.
I regret that I couldn't.

133
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:11,375
Life is full of surprises,
including the people we meet.

134
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:13,000
Like Uncle meeting her?

135
00:08:13,041 --> 00:08:15,375
Don't even mention that.
My head is killing me.

136
00:08:16,895 --> 00:08:18,686
What's your recruitment plan?

137
00:08:18,750 --> 00:08:20,250
At the moment, we only have Tae O.

138
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:23,791
I know. That's why I have a favor to ask.

139
00:08:24,125 --> 00:08:25,125
What is it?

140
00:08:25,928 --> 00:08:27,864
I'll ask Na Ji Ni to work with us.

141
00:08:28,469 --> 00:08:31,428
First, I'll finish the children's book
Ji Ni and Tae O were working on.

142
00:08:31,876 --> 00:08:35,482
Then I'll adapt the completed book
into an animated series.

143
00:08:36,178 --> 00:08:39,603
To do that, I absolutely need Ji Ni.
She created the original characters.

144
00:08:40,401 --> 00:08:42,151
Do Hee will get the wrong idea.

145
00:08:42,250 --> 00:08:43,416
Please keep her from interfering, Dad.

146
00:08:43,625 --> 00:08:44,666
Do you really have to do this?

147
00:08:44,875 --> 00:08:46,875
Many people are as capable as Ji Ni.

148
00:08:48,016 --> 00:08:49,874
- Is it like your mom said...
- No, Dad.

149
00:08:49,875 --> 00:08:52,091
This is only about work.
You have to believe me.

150
00:08:54,375 --> 00:08:55,927
Has Ji Ni agreed to work with you?

151
00:08:56,009 --> 00:08:57,040
I'm working on convincing her.

152
00:08:57,351 --> 00:08:59,810
We also need to bring in more people.

153
00:09:07,323 --> 00:09:08,614
If you two are okay with it...

154
00:09:08,625 --> 00:09:10,500
I'm definitely going with you.

155
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:11,750
Me too.

156
00:09:11,875 --> 00:09:14,875
The new director doesn't know anything.

157
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:16,621
He picks on me all the time.

158
00:09:16,625 --> 00:09:18,250
He's having a really hard time.

159
00:09:19,152 --> 00:09:22,339
Anyway, there's the size of the company
and how it looks on a business card.

160
00:09:22,654 --> 00:09:24,168
And most importantly, the salary.

161
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:26,750
Think it over and get back to me.

162
00:09:27,463 --> 00:09:29,588
Honestly, I've thought about it.

163
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:33,250
I'd rather struggle on payday
than struggle every single day.

164
00:09:33,375 --> 00:09:34,916
That's very persuasive.

165
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:38,789
But who'll handle the illustrations?
It's the most important thing.

166
00:09:38,823 --> 00:09:41,600
We're working on it now.
You'll be surprised when you find out.

167
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:44,791
Who could it be?

168
00:09:51,469 --> 00:09:52,819
Is this the office?

169
00:09:53,375 --> 00:09:55,050
Yeah. Long time no see.

170
00:09:55,625 --> 00:09:56,791
How's the filming going?

171
00:09:57,645 --> 00:09:58,936
Pretty well, I guess.

172
00:09:59,171 --> 00:10:00,421
No filming today?

173
00:10:01,375 --> 00:10:05,541
I don't know if I should say this,
but we're delayed because of Do Hee.

174
00:10:06,717 --> 00:10:09,124
- "Because of Do Hee?"
- I heard she has a bruise on her face.

175
00:10:09,158 --> 00:10:11,949
That girl could at least
make her lies believable.

176
00:10:12,375 --> 00:10:14,750
Who knows?
Maybe she got into a fight somewhere.

177
00:10:15,625 --> 00:10:17,916
Or, if you ask me,
she had plastic surgery.

178
00:10:18,125 --> 00:10:20,375
A bad injection can leave bruises
on your face.

179
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,456
I heard you're unemployed.

180
00:10:27,375 --> 00:10:29,041
Yes, I am.

181
00:10:29,706 --> 00:10:32,290
Want to come hang out with Ji Ni tomorrow?

182
00:10:32,587 --> 00:10:33,587
Me?

183
00:10:34,034 --> 00:10:35,274
Come cheer me on.

184
00:10:38,421 --> 00:10:39,421
Okay.

185
00:10:46,875 --> 00:10:51,125
Excuse me, is the owner around?

186
00:10:51,455 --> 00:10:55,414
Yes, someone's here. Just a moment.

187
00:11:02,250 --> 00:11:05,916
Yes? What are you looking for?

188
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:08,916
Ji Ni!

189
00:11:10,416 --> 00:11:11,560
What's this?

190
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,125
Why aren't you saying anything?

191
00:11:16,166 --> 00:11:18,207
Jung A, seriously!

192
00:11:20,041 --> 00:11:21,250
Wait here a minute.

193
00:11:39,875 --> 00:11:41,375
Enjoy your meal.

194
00:11:44,942 --> 00:11:46,612
That looks delicious.

195
00:11:48,250 --> 00:11:49,375
What's so funny?

196
00:11:51,291 --> 00:11:55,875
After I had you,
I got an earful from Yeong Ju,

197
00:11:55,916 --> 00:11:57,625
and your grandma collapsed.

198
00:11:58,166 --> 00:12:01,322
Compared to back then,
I can handle anything now.

199
00:12:02,250 --> 00:12:03,875
Don't make me feel miserable.

200
00:12:04,375 --> 00:12:05,875
Whenever you bring that up,

201
00:12:07,250 --> 00:12:10,425
all I can think is that I burdened you...

202
00:12:11,166 --> 00:12:12,375
and made your life miserable.

203
00:12:12,416 --> 00:12:13,700
That's not what I mean.

204
00:12:13,875 --> 00:12:17,419
I got through those dark years
because I had you.

205
00:12:17,625 --> 00:12:19,000
Don't think that way.

206
00:12:21,041 --> 00:12:22,125
Okay.

207
00:12:23,375 --> 00:12:27,291
By the way, I asked Seung Woo
to take over your dad's company.

208
00:12:27,750 --> 00:12:28,750
Will he do it?

209
00:12:30,041 --> 00:12:31,875
I'll have to keep talking to him.

210
00:12:32,811 --> 00:12:36,520
Don't take on more part-time jobs.
Just focus on your art.

211
00:12:36,625 --> 00:12:39,416
Your dad always said your art
has a way of comforting people.

212
00:12:39,666 --> 00:12:42,625
And you have to make that animation.
It's your dad's dying wish.

213
00:12:43,171 --> 00:12:46,160
And make my wish come true too.
Have a beautiful wedding.

214
00:12:46,583 --> 00:12:47,666
There you go again.

215
00:12:48,541 --> 00:12:52,415
And be careful with that director.
Don't let people start talking.

216
00:12:52,416 --> 00:12:53,541
I know.

217
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:56,625
Anyway, you can't stay here
for more than an hour.

218
00:12:57,875 --> 00:13:00,686
You're 80 percent of my worries.

219
00:13:01,908 --> 00:13:02,908
You little brat.

220
00:13:07,750 --> 00:13:09,166
It's delicious.

221
00:13:11,875 --> 00:13:13,125
I'm a little hurt.

222
00:13:13,375 --> 00:13:14,375
About what?

223
00:13:15,125 --> 00:13:17,125
A bottle of Chinese liquor, please.

224
00:13:18,375 --> 00:13:20,250
- Drink, but no black bean noodles.
- Hey!

225
00:13:21,291 --> 00:13:22,374
That's not fair.

226
00:13:22,375 --> 00:13:25,625
Your hands shake from all that drinking.

227
00:13:26,375 --> 00:13:27,500
It's this hand.

228
00:13:32,435 --> 00:13:34,101
It's delicious.

229
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:48,600
It's been rough, right?

230
00:13:49,125 --> 00:13:50,375
A little exhausting.

231
00:13:50,625 --> 00:13:52,625
It's my first time looking for a place.

232
00:13:52,864 --> 00:13:55,198
- What?
- I never had the chance.

233
00:13:55,476 --> 00:14:00,060
I lived with my parents till I wed at 23,
and I've lived here ever since.

234
00:14:01,416 --> 00:14:02,875
I see.

235
00:14:04,908 --> 00:14:06,658
You liked the last house best, right?

236
00:14:06,666 --> 00:14:10,666
I liked it, but didn't it have many rooms?

237
00:14:10,783 --> 00:14:11,993
Four is too many.

238
00:14:12,625 --> 00:14:16,416
One for us, one for Seung Hyun
and Seung Woo when they stay over,

239
00:14:16,875 --> 00:14:20,625
one as a dressing room
for all the things I buy you,

240
00:14:20,666 --> 00:14:23,763
and one soundproof room
for you to practice singing.

241
00:14:24,282 --> 00:14:28,948
Wait. Once Seung Woo gets married,
we'll have more family,

242
00:14:29,250 --> 00:14:31,750
so one guest room won't be enough.

243
00:14:31,867 --> 00:14:34,783
- Should we get a two-story house?
- Forget it.

244
00:14:35,041 --> 00:14:37,500
Why would we need a two-story house
for just the two of us?

245
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,166
"Just the two of us?"

246
00:14:41,074 --> 00:14:42,533
I love the sound of that.

247
00:14:44,250 --> 00:14:46,041
Is this really your first time?

248
00:14:46,502 --> 00:14:50,112
You want to get married this badly.
How have you been single all this time?

249
00:14:50,250 --> 00:14:52,125
I'm wondering that myself.

250
00:14:52,166 --> 00:14:56,373
I never knew I wanted marriage this badly.

251
00:14:59,046 --> 00:15:00,520
How are things with Seung Woo?

252
00:15:00,791 --> 00:15:05,125
He left early this morning.
I didn't get to see him.

253
00:15:07,283 --> 00:15:09,824
Don't worry. He's my son.

254
00:15:10,219 --> 00:15:14,094
In the end, all my sons
just want me to be happy.

255
00:15:14,625 --> 00:15:18,166
Once they realize
how much energy you give me,

256
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:20,791
they'll treat you even better.

257
00:15:21,546 --> 00:15:25,921
Seung Woo was always like a friend to me.

258
00:15:26,231 --> 00:15:28,897
Could I meet him?

259
00:15:29,291 --> 00:15:31,666
I'm a little worried about it right now.

260
00:15:32,219 --> 00:15:33,928
Seung Woo is strong-willed.

261
00:15:34,094 --> 00:15:36,678
Don't worry. If he hits me, I'll take it.

262
00:15:37,066 --> 00:15:39,107
That's how we'll bond.

263
00:15:40,489 --> 00:15:41,573
I'll ask him.

264
00:15:41,625 --> 00:15:45,250
If you want,
I can move into your house too.

265
00:15:45,416 --> 00:15:48,291
If your sons don't want
to be separated from you.

266
00:15:49,350 --> 00:15:50,434
No way.

267
00:15:50,666 --> 00:15:52,749
You want me to start married life
with my two sons?

268
00:15:52,750 --> 00:15:57,625
If that makes you comfortable.
Wait, "married life?"

269
00:16:00,416 --> 00:16:01,625
So sweet.

270
00:16:04,250 --> 00:16:05,500
Seriously!

271
00:16:10,541 --> 00:16:11,625
Your new home?

272
00:16:11,666 --> 00:16:14,000
Yeah, we went to look at some places.

273
00:16:14,291 --> 00:16:15,791
You don't have to worry.

274
00:16:17,697 --> 00:16:20,652
- Mom, you really went through with it...
- My brother and his wife...

275
00:16:21,125 --> 00:16:24,314
will never bother her again.

276
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:26,375
I'll keep her safe in a secure home.

277
00:16:27,750 --> 00:16:30,500
If that still worries you,
can I move in here with you?

278
00:16:30,625 --> 00:16:33,125
Move in here? You?

279
00:16:33,428 --> 00:16:34,844
I don't mind where we live.

280
00:16:35,541 --> 00:16:37,500
You're such a nice man!

281
00:16:37,875 --> 00:16:40,791
I hate nice men.

282
00:16:40,875 --> 00:16:43,500
You're nice to everyone.
You should only be nice to my mom.

283
00:16:44,125 --> 00:16:46,749
How can I trust a man
who can't protect his own people?

284
00:16:46,750 --> 00:16:48,041
Seung Woo.

285
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:49,750
I'm not a nice man.

286
00:16:50,428 --> 00:16:52,344
If I were, I'd have married someone...

287
00:16:52,601 --> 00:16:54,314
my brother and his wife introduced me to.

288
00:16:55,171 --> 00:16:56,796
I was looking for just one person.

289
00:16:57,409 --> 00:16:59,439
I didn't know it would be Yeong Ju,
but now I do.

290
00:17:00,497 --> 00:17:04,331
Even if I have to cut ties with my family,
I'll protect her.

291
00:17:04,333 --> 00:17:05,625
You have to trust me.

292
00:17:05,803 --> 00:17:07,219
Then cut ties with us too, Mom.

293
00:17:08,087 --> 00:17:10,046
- How can you...
- She can't.

294
00:17:10,797 --> 00:17:13,797
If you don't accept me,
she won't come to me.

295
00:17:14,125 --> 00:17:15,750
Sa Bin.

296
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:17,547
Can you come with me?

297
00:17:18,875 --> 00:17:21,625
How could she cut ties with her sons?
She can't do that.

298
00:17:22,625 --> 00:17:23,916
I can't go along with that.

299
00:17:25,963 --> 00:17:27,172
Do whatever you want.

300
00:17:27,625 --> 00:17:31,750
I can't stop you. Looks like you two
have already been house hunting. Go ahead.

301
00:17:32,087 --> 00:17:33,260
I'm not against it anymore.

302
00:17:44,625 --> 00:17:47,125
That's enough. Go. It'll get better.

303
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,375
I told you before.

304
00:17:50,003 --> 00:17:52,712
When I'm happy, the kids feel reassured.

305
00:17:53,303 --> 00:17:56,928
They're hurt because they've seen
how unhappy I've been all these years.

306
00:18:21,553 --> 00:18:24,527
If you're going crazy, do it quietly.
What? You want to disown me?

307
00:18:24,750 --> 00:18:26,000
Do you even know what that means?

308
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:30,450
What else can I do?
When have I ever done this?

309
00:18:30,750 --> 00:18:33,166
I've only decided to get married once.

310
00:18:33,884 --> 00:18:36,343
But how can you oppose me like this?

311
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:38,041
You're my only brother too.

312
00:18:38,625 --> 00:18:42,000
I'm so hurt and disappointed that...

313
00:18:42,375 --> 00:18:45,165
even if I can't marry Yeong Ju,
I want to disown you.

314
00:18:45,166 --> 00:18:47,250
- Im Sa Bin!
- Seriously.

315
00:18:48,527 --> 00:18:52,527
You even went to her place
and hit her. Why would you do that?

316
00:18:53,567 --> 00:18:57,901
Seriously, why? Is it because
I'm not marrying that 35-year-old woman?

317
00:18:57,916 --> 00:19:00,290
Anyone can see she's much better.

318
00:19:00,291 --> 00:19:03,750
Who cares what others think?
I'm the one who has to like her.

319
00:19:03,875 --> 00:19:06,169
Yeong Ju makes me feel better.

320
00:19:06,170 --> 00:19:08,750
I feel at ease when I'm with her.

321
00:19:09,750 --> 00:19:12,397
Are you all that matters? Tell me!

322
00:19:14,912 --> 00:19:18,540
No offense, but my sister isn't for you.

323
00:19:18,541 --> 00:19:22,041
Seriously, a brother shouldn't
act like that.

324
00:19:22,418 --> 00:19:24,760
Why did you go there and yell at her?

325
00:19:25,125 --> 00:19:28,506
Did she seduce me? I pursued her.

326
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,374
Just try going back there again.

327
00:19:31,375 --> 00:19:34,791
- I'll stop you myself.
- Doctor.

328
00:19:35,625 --> 00:19:37,375
So you're looking at houses?

329
00:19:39,541 --> 00:19:40,867
Don't come to the wedding.

330
00:19:41,250 --> 00:19:43,322
If you're going to act like this,
don't come at all.

331
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:45,166
Sa Bin.

332
00:19:45,291 --> 00:19:47,875
Joong Bin, choose. Your wife or me?

333
00:19:48,158 --> 00:19:50,955
If you'll convince your wife
and come with a smile, you're welcome.

334
00:19:51,317 --> 00:19:52,625
Otherwise, disown me.

335
00:19:52,750 --> 00:19:53,750
Sa Bin!

336
00:19:58,875 --> 00:20:03,041
This is ridiculous. Absolutely insane.

337
00:20:03,375 --> 00:20:04,989
I've never seen anything like this,
not even in a drama.

338
00:20:05,375 --> 00:20:11,291
At 50, no less.
I don't even know what to say.

339
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:30,619
No Yeong Ju, you really...

340
00:20:34,178 --> 00:20:36,573
Now you're going to be cooking
in the same kitchen as your sister-in-law.

341
00:20:37,408 --> 00:20:38,408
What?

342
00:20:39,421 --> 00:20:40,421
What did you say?

343
00:20:41,008 --> 00:20:44,032
It's because I went there
and hit her with flowers.

344
00:20:45,398 --> 00:20:51,495
If we part ways now, I don't know
when I'll be on good terms with him again.

345
00:20:52,250 --> 00:20:57,250
A sister-in-law...
I don't want to say this, but...

346
00:20:58,165 --> 00:21:03,421
Looks like someone I went to school with
will be my sister-in-law.

347
00:21:04,173 --> 00:21:07,791
So I'll accept it
and try to get along with her.

348
00:21:08,375 --> 00:21:14,166
- Honey.
- I really went there for Sa Bin.

349
00:21:15,125 --> 00:21:17,000
I just didn't think this was right.

350
00:21:17,541 --> 00:21:18,625
I know.

351
00:21:20,125 --> 00:21:22,125
I feel the same way you do.

352
00:21:24,875 --> 00:21:29,875
Honey, think about letting
her move in with us.

353
00:21:30,350 --> 00:21:33,100
I can't let you lose your brother
because of me.

354
00:21:34,291 --> 00:21:35,291
Honey.

355
00:21:37,750 --> 00:21:38,900
Sun Kyung.

356
00:21:40,665 --> 00:21:43,581
I'll do whatever it takes
to make this work.

357
00:21:44,125 --> 00:21:48,125
I had dreams of my own
for when my sister-in-law moved in,

358
00:21:50,404 --> 00:21:52,529
but I never thought
it'd turn out like this.

359
00:21:53,935 --> 00:21:58,560
With Do Hee joining us, and Sa Bin
getting married and having a baby...

360
00:21:59,608 --> 00:22:03,483
I thought our family would grow this year.

361
00:22:05,566 --> 00:22:08,941
That was my dream every New Year too.

362
00:22:18,870 --> 00:22:21,620
- Come on, follow me.
- Let go.

363
00:22:21,625 --> 00:22:22,875
Come on.

364
00:22:24,041 --> 00:22:25,125
I said let go.

365
00:22:25,791 --> 00:22:27,875
- Hey, you...
- Come with me.

366
00:22:27,967 --> 00:22:29,883
- I'm looking here.
- I've already looked here.

367
00:22:30,790 --> 00:22:33,206
She's not here. Come on.

368
00:22:35,875 --> 00:22:36,943
What the...

369
00:22:45,114 --> 00:22:46,198
How did you find me?

370
00:22:46,431 --> 00:22:48,306
I went around to clubs looking for Mai.

371
00:22:48,684 --> 00:22:50,809
I checked every place
on the list you wrote down too.

372
00:22:52,073 --> 00:22:56,157
I got such bad dark circles
from all that club-hopping. Can't you see?

373
00:22:56,330 --> 00:22:58,539
Why bother looking for me? I'm not a kid.

374
00:22:58,541 --> 00:23:01,291
If you're not a kid, why
do you keep giving mom such a hard time?

375
00:23:03,166 --> 00:23:04,416
Did you go to Vietnam?

376
00:23:07,875 --> 00:23:09,541
Where on earth is she?

377
00:23:12,810 --> 00:23:15,726
Mom's getting married.
You have to come to the wedding.

378
00:23:17,750 --> 00:23:18,750
You go.

379
00:23:19,684 --> 00:23:23,309
I saw mom drinking alone
at a street food stall.

380
00:23:23,851 --> 00:23:26,818
She said you used to stay by her side
and look after her when we were young.

381
00:23:28,160 --> 00:23:33,047
Seeing Mom there alone, I wondered,
was her back always that small?

382
00:23:34,625 --> 00:23:35,666
Are you finally growing up?

383
00:23:36,509 --> 00:23:40,038
I never realized before
how small mom really is.

384
00:23:41,536 --> 00:23:43,286
We're mom's family to lean on now.

385
00:23:43,416 --> 00:23:48,000
We need to stand by her and show her
we won't let anyone mess with her.

386
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:53,867
Once you move out and mom leaves too,

387
00:23:54,151 --> 00:23:58,526
will it just be Ji Ni's family and me?
That's horrifying. I get chills.

388
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:02,562
- I'll think about it.
- Pick up when I call.

389
00:24:03,509 --> 00:24:04,650
If you don't, I'm not going.

390
00:24:08,125 --> 00:24:09,250
Okay.

391
00:24:24,199 --> 00:24:26,033
Let's meet at lunch if you have time.

392
00:24:26,719 --> 00:24:28,084
Sun Kyung wants to apologize.

393
00:24:29,041 --> 00:24:30,041
Joong Bin.

394
00:24:41,625 --> 00:24:42,692
Your brother?

395
00:24:44,303 --> 00:24:47,594
Yes. No, it's okay.

396
00:24:48,500 --> 00:24:51,000
Okay. Yeah.

397
00:25:04,134 --> 00:25:05,372
You're here, Yeong Ju?

398
00:25:05,803 --> 00:25:07,928
This family tree is getting complicated.

399
00:25:09,125 --> 00:25:12,375
- Hello.
- Come in. Good to see you.

400
00:25:15,500 --> 00:25:18,249
You two were schoolmates.
No need to be formal. Right, Sun Kyung?

401
00:25:18,250 --> 00:25:20,500
Of course. Come sit down.

402
00:25:20,541 --> 00:25:22,250
Yeah, have a seat.

403
00:25:26,375 --> 00:25:29,125
I'm sorry about last time.

404
00:25:29,750 --> 00:25:30,821
It's okay.

405
00:25:32,809 --> 00:25:33,934
This is heartwarming.

406
00:25:35,969 --> 00:25:37,428
Welcome. We're glad to have you.

407
00:25:38,114 --> 00:25:41,069
It's nice to meet you. I'm No Yeong Ju.

408
00:25:47,046 --> 00:25:50,962
I apologize for everything that happened
while we opposed the marriage.

409
00:25:51,955 --> 00:25:56,075
Because of that, my brother and I
hurt each other like never before.

410
00:25:56,851 --> 00:25:57,935
I'm sorry.

411
00:25:58,046 --> 00:26:02,212
Hey, you don't have to bring that up.
You're making Yeong Ju uncomfortable.

412
00:26:02,250 --> 00:26:03,541
Let him speak.

413
00:26:04,375 --> 00:26:05,500
Go ahead.

414
00:26:06,087 --> 00:26:08,212
So my wife and I thought...

415
00:26:08,904 --> 00:26:12,529
that if we parted ways with Sa Bin,
considering how close we've grown,

416
00:26:12,625 --> 00:26:15,595
and with you being new to the family,
we'd feel too distant from you.

417
00:26:16,500 --> 00:26:22,250
So we'd like to live together for a year
before living separately.

418
00:26:22,291 --> 00:26:23,291
What?

419
00:26:23,968 --> 00:26:28,189
Yeong Ju, I don't want
to lose Sa Bin over this.

420
00:26:28,719 --> 00:26:30,553
We've had so many misunderstandings.

421
00:26:31,594 --> 00:26:33,678
Let's spend some time together.

422
00:26:35,250 --> 00:26:37,586
I understand how you feel, but we can't.

423
00:26:37,587 --> 00:26:39,034
We're going to live on our own.

424
00:26:39,401 --> 00:26:41,901
Joong Bin,
what kind of ridiculous idea is that?

425
00:26:44,351 --> 00:26:48,935
Sa Bin, I'm working up the courage
to say this right now.

426
00:26:50,427 --> 00:26:55,047
Do you really hate the idea?
Would you rather cut ties and leave?

427
00:26:55,791 --> 00:26:57,916
Well, I...

428
00:26:58,047 --> 00:27:00,422
Never mind.

429
00:27:01,541 --> 00:27:03,666
We're adults. Why should we live together?

430
00:27:04,125 --> 00:27:05,916
Do you always have to do things your way?

431
00:27:06,388 --> 00:27:08,888
She's asking this much of you.
Why are you being so stubborn?

432
00:27:09,249 --> 00:27:11,748
With our parents gone,
do we really have to live apart like this?

433
00:27:11,750 --> 00:27:13,375
Why are you getting angry all of a sudden?

434
00:27:14,502 --> 00:27:16,685
If you're going to interfere like this,
then let's live apart.

435
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:18,500
You should've done that from the start.

436
00:27:18,783 --> 00:27:21,199
Yeong Ju, let's go.
There's nothing more to hear.

437
00:27:21,250 --> 00:27:22,750
- Sa Bin.
- We're not done talking.

438
00:27:23,166 --> 00:27:25,041
- Where are you going? We're not done.
- What are you doing?

439
00:27:25,125 --> 00:27:28,000
Why are you holding her hand? Let go!

440
00:27:28,125 --> 00:27:30,500
Yeong Ju, just give us one year.

441
00:27:30,541 --> 00:27:33,875
Why are you being so pathetic?
This is ridiculous.

442
00:27:34,541 --> 00:27:37,166
- Yeong Ju.
- Let go. Seriously!

443
00:27:37,625 --> 00:27:40,915
What are you doing? Let go of her hand.

444
00:27:40,916 --> 00:27:43,249
- You're going to tear her clothes.
- What are you doing?

445
00:27:43,250 --> 00:27:44,537
Wait a minute.

446
00:28:03,375 --> 00:28:06,665
(Family Register)

447
00:28:06,666 --> 00:28:09,999
No Yeong Ju, how dare you
try to become part of my family?

448
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:12,999
What can I do? I don't want that.

449
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:16,250
How long are you going to live
in Ji Ni's shadow, you pathetic servant?

450
00:28:16,291 --> 00:28:18,041
She tried to split my lip open.

451
00:28:18,125 --> 00:28:19,249
Do Hee did this to me.

452
00:28:19,250 --> 00:28:21,750
Do you have proof Do Hee did it?
What makes you say that?

453
00:28:21,791 --> 00:28:25,166
Honey, you don't have to worry
about Yeong Ju anymore.

454
00:28:27,200 --> 00:28:29,200
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
